  "courseSlug": "nextjs-react-the-complete-guide",
  "courseTitle": "Next.js & React - The Complete Guide",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "25145594",
      "title": "Extracting Data on the Catch-All Page",
      "lectureOrder": 259,
      "videoOrder": 241,
      "sourceHash": "f8617e0ea8b983b0de97cdb44243a27bb55d0f3cb171a8de36ef057f91b893ec",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.04,
          "end": 5.16,
          "en": "So let's now display our Filtered Events",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 5.16,
          "end": 8.32,
          "en": "let's work on this slug page therefore.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 8.32,
          "end": 11.46,
          "en": "On this page, we now got a couple of things to do.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 11.46,
          "end": 16.29,
          "en": "We need to extract the dynamic segment values",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 16.29,
          "end": 20.06,
          "en": "which are part of the URL that led to this page.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 20.06,
          "end": 22.59,
          "en": "And we need to extract the year and the month",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 22.59,
          "end": 27.59,
          "en": "and then find the events that meet this year and month.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 27.8,
          "end": 29.82,
          "en": "Now in the dummy-data js file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 29.82,
          "end": 33.88,
          "en": "I already prepared a \"getFilteredEvents\" function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 34.99,
          "end": 38.57,
          "en": "which expects an object with a year and the month key",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 38.57,
          "end": 42.68,
          "en": "where I then look for the events that have the respect",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 42.68,
          "end": 45.28,
          "en": "of year and month, and they need to have both.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 45.28,
          "end": 50.09,
          "en": "So this is not an \"or\" filter, but an \"and\" filter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 50.09,
          "end": 51.79,
          "en": "I'm looking for events that have",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 51.79,
          "end": 55.13,
          "en": "both the selected year and the selected month.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 55.13,
          "end": 57.29,
          "en": "So that logic is already in place.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 57.29,
          "end": 58.74,
          "en": "But in the slug component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 58.74,
          "end": 62.51,
          "en": "we now need to extract the data from the URL.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 62.51,
          "end": 66.53,
          "en": "And for this, we again can use to useRouter hook.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 66.53,
          "end": 68.55,
          "en": "This gives us access to the data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 68.55,
          "end": 73.13,
          "en": "encoded in the URL and this slug page is no exception.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 73.13,
          "end": 76.337,
          "en": "So here we now import useRouter from nextRouter",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 77.64,
          "end": 79.57,
          "en": "and then we create our router object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 79.57,
          "end": 81.863,
          "en": "by calling useRouter like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 83,
          "end": 85.93,
          "en": "Now here we can get our \"filterData\"",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 85.93,
          "end": 89.78,
          "en": "by accessing router.query.slug.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 89.78,
          "end": 92.21000000000001,
          "en": "But what is that \"filterData\"?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 92.21000000000001,
          "end": 94.15,
          "en": "Well, let's recall what it is",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 94.15,
          "end": 98.44,
          "en": "by quickly logging it to the console that \"filterData\".",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 98.44,
          "end": 100.53,
          "en": "Let's log it to the console.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 100.53,
          "end": 103.38,
          "en": "Go back here to this events page",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 103.38,
          "end": 108.38,
          "en": "to this Filtered Events page for events/2021/5",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 108.59,
          "end": 110.82,
          "en": "and open the dev tools and reload.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 110.82,
          "end": 113.02000000000001,
          "en": "And we see that it's such an array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 113.02000000000001,
          "end": 115.41,
          "en": "It's an array with two elements.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 115.41,
          "end": 118.21000000000001,
          "en": "And the first element is the first segment,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 118.21000000000001,
          "end": 120.74,
          "en": "the second element is the second segment.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 120.74,
          "end": 122.23,
          "en": "And if we had more segments",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 122.23,
          "end": 124.78,
          "en": "we would have more items in that array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 124.78,
          "end": 127.63,
          "en": "We also have \"undefined\" being logged here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 127.63,
          "end": 131.8,
          "en": "because actually this component is rendered twice,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 131.8,
          "end": 133.78,
          "en": "because of how React works",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 133.78,
          "end": 136.82,
          "en": "and how that route data is extracted.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 136.82,
          "end": 140.6,
          "en": "Effectively, this hook extracting the route data,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 140.6,
          "end": 144.55,
          "en": "runs after the component was rendered for the first time.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 144.55,
          "end": 146.96,
          "en": "So the first time the component renders",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 146.96,
          "end": 150.65,
          "en": "we don't have access to that URL data yet.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 150.65,
          "end": 152.64,
          "en": "That's not a problem per se",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 152.64,
          "end": 154.65,
          "en": "but we'll have to make sure that we only",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 154.65,
          "end": 157.97,
          "en": "look for Filtered Events once we got access",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 157.97,
          "end": 159.623,
          "en": "to the URL data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 160.746,
          "end": 162.9,
          "en": "And in additional, of course we want to make sure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 162.9,
          "end": 164.82999999999998,
          "en": "that we don't try to look for events",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 164.82999999999998,
          "end": 169.28,
          "en": "if there is a third parameter, if there is \"abc\" at the end",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 169.28,
          "end": 171.13,
          "en": "or at least we don't want to include",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 171.13,
          "end": 175.483,
          "en": "that in our query, in our filter logic.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 176.4,
          "end": 180.27,
          "en": "So to make sure that this works appropriately,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 180.27,
          "end": 184.3,
          "en": "I'll first of all, check if filter data is faulty",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 184.3,
          "end": 186.12,
          "en": "by adding an exclamation mark here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 186.12,
          "end": 188.37,
          "en": "so that when it is undefined",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 188.37,
          "end": 190.84,
          "en": "which it will be when the component is rendered",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 190.84,
          "end": 194.47,
          "en": "for the first time, it's then automatically rendered again.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 194.47,
          "end": 197.21,
          "en": "But it is rendered without filter data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 197.21,
          "end": 199.18,
          "en": "when it is rendered for the first time.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 199.18,
          "end": 201.57,
          "en": "And when that happens, I want to return",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 201.57,
          "end": 206.28,
          "en": "let's say a paragraph where I say \"loading...\"",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 206.28,
          "end": 210.63,
          "en": "We can give this paragraph a class name of \"center\".",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 210.63,
          "end": 212.49,
          "en": "And here that's regular string",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 212.49,
          "end": 216.51,
          "en": "because that is a globally defined CSS clause",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 216.51,
          "end": 219.23,
          "en": "in the global CSS file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 219.23,
          "end": 221.64,
          "en": "So here it's a regular string, which I set",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 221.64,
          "end": 225.34,
          "en": "as a clause named to apply this global CSS clause.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 225.34,
          "end": 227.32999999999998,
          "en": "So not a scope clause.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 227.32999999999998,
          "end": 230.85,
          "en": "And with that, we take care that we don't get an error,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 230.85,
          "end": 235.023,
          "en": "just because we don't have access to the URL data yet.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 236.16,
          "end": 237.94,
          "en": "That's simply how to use,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 237.94,
          "end": 240.9,
          "en": "the router hook works internally.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 240.9,
          "end": 242.01,
          "en": "But now of course",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 242.01,
          "end": 244.66,
          "en": "when the component is then automatically rendered",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 244.66,
          "end": 247.73,
          "en": "for the second time, we do have access to the data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 247.73,
          "end": 249.81,
          "en": "And therefore now we do want to look",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 249.81,
          "end": 251.683,
          "en": "for the appropriate events.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 252.82,
          "end": 256.09,
          "en": "For this, I'm only interested in the first two segments",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 256.09,
          "end": 258.93,
          "en": "which I know will be the year and the month.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 258.93,
          "end": 263.21,
          "en": "So I'll get my \"filteredYear\" by accessing \"filterData\"",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 263.21,
          "end": 267.11,
          "en": "the first element, and we get the \"filteredMonth\"",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 267.11,
          "end": 270.553,
          "en": "by accessing the second element with index one.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 272.5,
          "end": 277.49,
          "en": "Now the data which we get here is in a string format.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 277.49,
          "end": 279.83,
          "en": "It's always a string because it's encoded",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 279.83,
          "end": 283.98,
          "en": "into URL and I need numbers.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 283.98,
          "end": 288.21,
          "en": "Therefore I'll set up my \"numbYear\"",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 288.21,
          "end": 290.44,
          "en": "by transforming \"filteredYear\"",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 290.44,
          "end": 292.94,
          "en": "to a number by adding a plus in front of it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 292.94,
          "end": 296.8,
          "en": "And the same year for the month with \"numbMonth\".",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 296.8,
          "end": 299.04,
          "en": "I transform this to a number",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 299.04,
          "end": 302.74,
          "en": "by adding a plus in front of \"filteredMonth\".",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 302.74,
          "end": 305.933,
          "en": "So that transforms that data to numbers.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 307.06,
          "end": 309.3,
          "en": "Now, of course, for some reason",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 309.3,
          "end": 312.56,
          "en": "we could fail to do that because for example",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 312.56,
          "end": 316.363,
          "en": "someone manually entered /events/abc/5.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 317.96,
          "end": 322.25,
          "en": "And in that case, 'abc\" would of course not be a valid year.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 322.25,
          "end": 325.48,
          "en": "So we also want to handle that scenario.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 325.48,
          "end": 327.12,
          "en": "And therefore I'll add a if-check",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 327.12,
          "end": 332.12,
          "en": "where I check if my \"numbYear\", so my year transformed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 332.56,
          "end": 336.18,
          "en": "to a number, is not a number which would happen",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 336.18,
          "end": 339.145,
          "en": "if that is a string like abc, for example",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 339.145,
          "end": 341.40999999999997,
          "en": "then we can't convert it to a number.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 341.40999999999997,
          "end": 345.61,
          "en": "And this year would produce \"not a number\" as a type.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 345.61,
          "end": 349.49,
          "en": "So I'll check if my \"numbYear\" is not a number",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 349.49,
          "end": 353.40999999999997,
          "en": "or if my \"numbMonth\" is not a number.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 353.40999999999997,
          "end": 354.87,
          "en": "If either of the two failed,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 354.87,
          "end": 357.433,
          "en": "something is wrong about that URL.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 358.6,
          "end": 361.93,
          "en": "I'll also check, as an additional condition",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 361.93,
          "end": 363.49,
          "en": "under which I want to fail,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 363.49,
          "end": 367.06,
          "en": "if my year let's say is greater than 2030,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 367.06,
          "end": 369.85,
          "en": "let's say that's the highest year I want to support,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 369.85,
          "end": 373.52,
          "en": "or if it's below 2021.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 373.52,
          "end": 377.81,
          "en": "And I'll also check if my month is maybe smaller than one,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 377.81,
          "end": 379.14,
          "en": "which makes no sense",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 379.14,
          "end": 381.62,
          "en": "or if the month is greater than 12",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 381.62,
          "end": 383.98,
          "en": "which also makes no sense.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 383.98,
          "end": 386.58,
          "en": "If either of these things is true,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 386.58,
          "end": 388.97,
          "en": "if either of these conditions is met",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 388.97,
          "end": 390.4,
          "en": "I don't want to continue",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 390.4,
          "end": 393.53,
          "en": "because then something is wrong with the filter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 393.53,
          "end": 397.1,
          "en": "So then I'll just return some output where I, for example",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 397.1,
          "end": 402.1,
          "en": "say \"Invalid filter. Please adjust your values!\"",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 404.56,
          "end": 406.5,
          "en": "So now with that, if we saved this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 406.5,
          "end": 411.5,
          "en": "and I would load this page for /events/abc5,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 411.51,
          "end": 415.407,
          "en": "I would get \"Invalid filter. Please adjust your values!\"",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 418.13,
          "end": 421.95,
          "en": "Now, assuming that we do have a valid year",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 421.95,
          "end": 426.75,
          "en": "and a valid month, I now can expect to find events though",
          "zh": ""
        },
